    "tactics": "Stone Soldiers advance steadily and hold ground. They will not pursue at speed; they outlast opposition rather than chase it. A summoner who needs something to simply not move will find them ideal.",
    "attacksNotes": "<p>Slam [Combat]: Melee attack (Agil 6 + Melee Combat 2), Reach: 5 ft</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Margin 1:</strong>: 10 damage (6 + 4 Str)</li>\n<li><strong>Margin 2:</strong> 10 damage, DR halved (round up)</li>\n<li><strong>Margin 3:</strong> 10 damage, DR halved (round up); target is knocked Prone</li>\n</ul>",
    "specialAbilitiesNotes": "<p>Immovable Mass: The Stone Soldier cannot be knocked Prone by any non-magical forced movement. Shoves and trips automatically fail unless the attacker wins an opposed Strength + Athletics check against the Soldier's Strength + Might (2 successes required). Gravel Rain: Once per encounter as a [Combat] action, the Stone Soldier slams the ground, sending a spray of rock fragments in a 10-foot cone. Creatures in area make a Reflex [Easy] save or take 8 bludgeoning damage (half on success). Full DR applies.</p>",
    "reactionsNotes": "<p>Stone Skin: [Reaction] once per round, Gain +2 DR against one attack.</p>",
